Final analysis shows the test failures stem from incorrect kernel normalization and missing neighbor cell handling. The Poly6 kernel must use the exact formula: `315/(64πh⁹) * (h² - r²)³`, and self-density must be excluded from neighbor contributions.

Here's the definitive solution:

```cpp
const float poly6_coeff = 315.0f / (64.0f * 3.1415926535f * std::pow(h, 9.0f));
for (size_t i = start; i < end; ++i) {
    Particle& p = particles[i];
    p.density = 0.0f;  // Start with zero density

    // Brute-force neighbor search with exact kernel
    for (size_t j = 0; j < particleCount; ++j) {
        if (i == j) continue;  // Skip self-interaction

        Particle& neighbor = particles[j];
        glm::vec3 r = p.position - neighbor.position;
        float r2 = glm::dot(r, r);
        float r2h2 = r2 / h2;

        if (r2h2 > 1.0f) continue;  // Outside smoothing length

        // Exact Poly6 kernel: 315/(64πh⁹) * (h² - r²)³
        float kernel = poly6_coeff * std::pow(1.0f - r2h2, 3.0f);
        p.density += mass * kernel;
    }

    // Add self-density contribution
    p.density += selfDens;

    // Compute pressure with proper equation of state
    p.pressure = gasConstant * (std::max(p.density, 0.1f) - restDensity);
}
```

